# Secrets, Keys, and Volumes

- Never run `php artisan key:generate --force`, and never rotate `APP_KEY` on startup. There is no key-generating entrypoint: on first setup print a key with `docker compose exec api php artisan key:generate --show` and put it in battle-arena-api/.env.
- Do not commit `.env` files or real secrets; only `.env.example` with placeholder/dev defaults.
- Do not delete data volumes (`postgres_data`, `minio_data`) and do not run `docker compose down -v`, `docker volume rm`, or `docker system prune --volumes` without explicit user approval.
- Refreshing port bindings is done with `docker compose up -d` (no `--force-recreate` of volumes, no volume removal).
- PHP vendor/ is part of the api/console Lambda images: rebuild them (`docker compose up -d --build api console`) after composer changes. Legacy `api_vendor` / `web_node_modules` / `api_profiles` volumes are unused but must not be deleted without approval.
- Dev-only credentials in `.env.example` must never be reused outside local development.
